<!--
Template SSIS package placeholder: Load_Amazon_CSV.dtsx

This file is a template description to import in Visual Studio and quickly build the real package.
It is not a binary .dtsx generated by Visual Studio. Follow the steps below to create the package exactly
as needed (fast and reliable):

1) In Visual Studio (SQL Server Data Tools) create a new Integration Services Project.
2) Add a new package and name it Load_Amazon_CSV.dtsx.
3) Create package Variables (ReadOnly/ReadWrite as indicated):
   - User::SourceFileName (String) default: C:\Users\eleag\Desktop\projetDW\Sources\csv\Amazon_SSIS.csv
   - User::PackageName (String) default: Load_Amazon_CSV
   - User::BatchID (Int32)
   - User::RowCount (Int32)
   - User::ErrorCount (Int32)
   - User::Status (String)

4) Create two Connection Managers:
   - Flat File Connection Manager named CSV_Amazon
     - FileName: use User::SourceFileName or set directly
     - Unicode: checked; Row delimiter {CR}{LF}; Column delimiter: ,; Text qualifier: " ; First row has column names
   - OLE DB Connection Manager named OLEDB_ProjDW
     - Provider: SQL Server Native Client or Microsoft OLE DB Driver
     - Connection string: point to your projetDW database

5) Control Flow design (in order):
   a) Execute SQL Task "InsertAuditStart"
      - SQL: INSERT INTO dbo.etl_control (SourceFileName, PackageName, StartTime, Status)
             VALUES (?, ?, SYSDATETIME(), 'Started');
      - Map parameters to User::SourceFileName, User::PackageName and capture SCOPE_IDENTITY() into User::BatchID

   b) Execute SQL Task (optional) "TruncateStaging" (run when truncateStaging = True)
      - SQL: TRUNCATE TABLE dbo.stg_Amazon;

   c) Data Flow Task "DFT_Load_Staging"
      - Components inside Data Flow:
         - Flat File Source (CSV_Amazon)
         - Data Conversion / Derived Column for data type cleaning
         - Conditional Split -> send bad rows to OLE DB Destination dbo.err_Amazon
         - OLE DB Destination (Fast Load) -> dbo.stg_Amazon

   d) Execute SQL Task "sp_Merge_Staging"
      - SQL: EXEC dbo.sp_Merge_Amazon_From_Staging;

   e) Execute SQL Task "UpdateAuditEnd"
      - SQL (use parameters): UPDATE dbo.etl_control SET EndTime = SYSDATETIME(), RowCount = ?, ErrorCount = ?, Status = ?, Message = ? WHERE BatchID = ?;
      - Map parameters from variables filled during package run

   f) Event handlers: OnError -> update etl_control Status = 'Failed' and set ErrorCount

6) Data flow performance settings and properties
   - OLE DB Destination: Use "Table or view - fast load", enable Table lock, set batch size according to file size
   - Configure DefaultBufferMaxRows/DefaultBufferSize if file large

7) Testing & Deployment
   - Test with small file first
   - Deploy to SSIS Catalog or save the package to a secured folder

This template describes the exact package to build. If you prefer, I can attempt to generate a fully formed .dtsx XML, but importing and validating it in Visual Studio is often faster by following the steps above.
-->
